ther big casualty of the finale his  human form is killed off by a host  version in that char Laura's built this  means that Ed Harris should continue to  have a starring role in the series but  human William is dead and sure Laura  says that he will save the world but  adds for us to the end of it referring  to the host some things to keep in mind  the Dolores mechanical body still exists  but the memories from her Dolores prime  build are gone there are still multiple  copies of her out there there's char  Loras there are the two pearls that were  in Connells and Musashi both of which  should be in Charla's possession now and  there is the one that was in the  Lawrence body whose  location is a mystery going into season  four none of these will amount to a  replacement of the character we've  watched Evan Rachel would play for three  seasons though whether or not this means  that Evan Rachel Wood will continue to  play a role in the series is unknown but  I will just throw it out there that dr.  Ford died at the end of season one and  that was not the last time we saw  Anthony Hopkins on screen the final  character left to discuss is Bernard or  more accurately Bern Arnold a  combination of the host named Bernard  that dr. Ford built and the man he was  based on Arnold Weber Ford's partner and  co-creator of the hosts it turns out  that Bernard was the one who had the key  that Ciroc had been looking for the  whole time he's visited by the Dolores  copy and Lawrence's body and given a  device that allows him to access the  sublime or the valley beyond he tells  Stubbs that he was wrong about Dolores  she wasn't trying to exterminate the  human race she was trying to save it he  says that mankind was always racing  towards this end in that what Ciroc and  his brother were doing was just holding  it off Stubbs calls it an apocalypse and  Bernard counters that the host had to  burn down their world to be free as well  he then uses the key to access the  sublime looking for an answer to the  question what comes after the end of the  world  so Bernhard survives and that keeps the  sublime safe it's also interesting to  remember that Bernard and by extension  the parts of Arnold that are inside this  host that we call Bernard now would in  fact remember Dolores prime and there's  definitely a chance that he could  rebuild her in the same way that she  rebuilt him  the final post-credit scene is Bernard  waking up in the same motel room covered  in enough dust to tell us he's been  there for some time we see him come back  online with no definitive answers for  how long he was gone or what he might  have learned in the valley beyond it's  an interesting question considering that  the valley beyond was created to give  the host who made it there like a catchy  taw and Teddy a world of their own to  build something free of human  influenced by going there he's going to  see what they came up with and Bernard  will definitely have something to share  with the world after he returns but it's  anyone's guess who will still be around  to share it with so to wrap things up  Kaleb and Maeve are alive and will  continue to see how the lorises Vision  plays out Ciroc was bleeding out the  last time we saw him but we didn't see  him die on screen so maybe he won't  Rehoboam his creation however has been  destroyed sure Loras has plans to make  sure that hosts survive we see that she  has a lot of resources but we don't know  what her endgame is that she has in mind  beyond just making sure that hosts  aren't exterminated from the planet  human man in black is dead but he has a  host version that lives on which is  under the control of sho Loras and  Dolores prime is gone but there's  several different ways where we may see  a different version and Evan Rachel  would return for season four and with  that I'll leave it there please like  this video if you enjoyed it tell me in  the comments what you thought of the  finale what you thought about season  three overall I liked the ending a lot  better than I liked the rest of the  season if I'm being honest it looks like  we're gonna have at least the season  four maybe going up to six seasons so  let me know what you think about that  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  I'll talk to you soon
 

